  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\mathrm{NO}_{2} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{N}_{2}+2 \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$\nVolume of $\\mathrm{N}_{2}$ formed in successive five minutes are $2.75 \\mathrm{cc}, 2.40 \\mathrm{cc}$ and $2.25 \\mathrm{cc}$ which is in decreasing order. So rate of reaction is dependent on concentration of $\\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\mathrm{NO}_{2}$. As decrease is not very fast so it will be first order reaction.",
